                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1771de6-14f6-3fb8-9f35-11fc4e39ceed",
                        "entry_id": "9aac1c32-c500-3bab-97f1-9e68ce122a1b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celui qui chicane, qui aime à chicaner, principalement en affaires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4eccb5b2-0a76-4f78-8101-03d6e09e510f",
                                "sense_id": "c1771de6-14f6-3fb8-9f35-11fc4e39ceed",
                                "text": "Et je gagne ma cause. A cela que fait-on ?\nMon chicaneur s'oppose à l'exécution."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "064358be-044f-4aae-a5a9-70c3dfa2b917",
                        "source_entry_id": "9aac1c32-c500-3bab-97f1-9e68ce122a1b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1771de6-14f6-3fb8-9f35-11fc4e39ceed",
                        "target_lang_word": "pettifogger",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pettifogger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cfc0f04-a91a-3d2c-8281-e8e5de904e1a",
                                        "entry_id": "c9065b12-d20a-3d9b-b313-bf4ce2a07a42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who quibbles over trivia, and raises petty, annoying objections and sophistry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "946dce9d-37f9-45c9-8418-5e5ee5662476",
                                                "sense_id": "4cfc0f04-a91a-3d2c-8281-e8e5de904e1a",
                                                "text": "Hence the cunning measure of appointing as ambassador some political pettifogger skilled in delays, sophisms, and misapprehensions, and dexterous in the art of baffling argument."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "608ac56c-ddb5-3164-a08f-313fbbab8241",
                                        "entry_id": "c9065b12-d20a-3d9b-b313-bf4ce2a07a42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unscrupulous or unethical lawyer, especially one of lesser skill."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2279d05a-2d49-446e-ad79-b78a2bd1a4e2",
                                                "sense_id": "608ac56c-ddb5-3164-a08f-313fbbab8241",
                                                "text": "\"An inn, or a tavern . . . these are places where greasy citizens take pipe and pot, where the knavish pettifoggers of the law spunge on their most unhappy victims."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4edbe070-f840-499b-bd8b-e74af1843532",
                                                "sense_id": "608ac56c-ddb5-3164-a08f-313fbbab8241",
                                                "text": "This gentleman (for such he was, however strange ladies who class country attorneys with vulgar pettifoggers in fashionable novels may deem the assertion) was the son of a brave officer,..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a761eb33-43c7-4ec3-8947-24dd544d9f42",
                                                "sense_id": "608ac56c-ddb5-3164-a08f-313fbbab8241",
                                                "text": ". . .yet he has never sought by browbeating and other arts of the pettifogger, to confuse, baffle, and bewilder a witness. . . ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a34aa4ce-ce25-427e-94cd-88dc6ad4d2ba",
                                                "sense_id": "608ac56c-ddb5-3164-a08f-313fbbab8241",
                                                "text": "\"Donald Hughes, well known in Minneapolis as a conscienceless shyster, was placed in charge of the case. . . . Mr. Edgerton, a high class, reputable lawyer, was called in of counsel from another city to lend respectability to the crooked, unprincipled, blackmailing pettifogger, Hughes.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3e436569-e5db-4cda-a1e4-89aa58ca1f41",
                        "source_entry_id": "9aac1c32-c500-3bab-97f1-9e68ce122a1b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1771de6-14f6-3fb8-9f35-11fc4e39ceed",
                        "target_lang_word": "shyster",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shyster",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                        "entry_id": "0df256a7-f10c-3fbb-9bd4-e4ca0706240f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who acts in a disreputable, unethical, or unscrupulous way, especially in the practice of law and politics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c6c2485-a39b-4fd5-b300-1e42cb5da435",
                                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                                "text": "True, it was a good advertisement at Boosters' Club lunches, and all the varieties of Annual Banquets to which Good Fellows were invited, to speak sonorously of […] a thing called Ethics, whose nature was confusing but if you had it you were a High-class Realtor and if you hadn't you were a shyster, a piker, and a fly-by-night."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07210c20-331e-4f6e-88fb-4320b9bcd863",
                                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                                "text": "The network canceled—nonco-operation their legal shysters said. Suing me, for, for ten million clams, damages to sponsors, agencies. Internal Revenue-Uncle Whiskers says I owe them a mint."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72bf798c-06e7-48ce-97b5-cba430794c0e",
                                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                                "text": "I could sue you, Polly. A shyster is a disreputable lawyer. I'm a quack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shyster",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "061ac99c-3248-350f-96c7-bd79f73ebbef",
